            <!-- I) MCQs -->
            <section id="mcq" class="card mb-3">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h5">MCQ (10)</h2>
                    <p class="soft">Click “Show Answer” to reveal the correct option and explanation.</p>

                    <div class="list-group">

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q1.</b> A web application is primarily accessed using:
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Command Prompt</div>
                                <div>B) Web Browser</div>
                                <div>C) Notepad</div>
                                <div>D) BIOS</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq1">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq1" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> B) Web Browser<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Web apps are designed to be used through URLs in a browser.
                                        The browser is the client that renders pages and sends requests.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q2.</b> In a web app, server-side C# code runs on:
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Browser</div>
                                <div>B) Server</div>
                                <div>C) Router</div>
                                <div>D) Monitor</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq2">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq2" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> B) Server<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Server-side languages run on the server.
                                        The browser receives final output such as HTML/JSON.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q3.</b> The most common communication cycle in web apps is:
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Request–Response</div>
                                <div>B) Bluetooth pairing</div>
                                <div>C) USB transfer</div>
                                <div>D) Offline-only processing</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq3">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq3" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Request–Response<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Browser sends an HTTP request; server returns an HTTP response.
                                        This powers pages, form submits, and API calls.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q4.</b> Which is a typical feature of web applications?
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Centralized updates</div>
                                <div>B) Runs only offline</div>
                                <div>C) Cannot integrate with APIs</div>
                                <div>D) Requires installation on every device</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq4">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq4" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Centralized updates<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        You deploy updates on the server once.
                                        All users get the new version automatically on refresh.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q5.</b> Which format is commonly returned for a normal web page?
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) HTML</div>
                                <div>B) BIOS settings</div>
                                <div>C) GPU drivers</div>
                                <div>D) Battery telemetry only</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq5">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq5" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) HTML<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Pages are typically HTML rendered by the server and displayed by the browser.
                                        APIs often return JSON instead.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q6.</b> Static websites usually:
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Provide fixed content</div>
                                <div>B) Always need login</div>
                                <div>C) Always use databases</div>
                                <div>D) Must use MVC</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq6">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq6" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Provide fixed content<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Static sites serve pre-built pages.
                                        Web applications usually generate content dynamically based on user actions and data.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q7.</b> Which is the best example of a web application?
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Online banking portal</div>
                                <div>B) A single static brochure page</div>
                                <div>C) Desktop-only calculator</div>
                                <div>D) BIOS utility</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq7">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq7" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Online banking portal<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Banking portals are interactive, dynamic, and database-driven.
                                        They include login, transactions, and role-based access.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q8.</b> Which protocol is commonly used by web apps?
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) HTTP/HTTPS</div>
                                <div>B) HDMI</div>
                                <div>C) VGA</div>
                                <div>D) SATA</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq8">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq8" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) HTTP/HTTPS<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        HTTP is the standard protocol for web communication.
                                        HTTPS is the secure encrypted version, required for modern web apps.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q9.</b> In web terminology, the browser is called the:
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Client</div>
                                <div>B) Database</div>
                                <div>C) Compiler</div>
                                <div>D) Web server</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq9">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq9" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Client<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Client requests resources and displays them.
                                        Server hosts the application and sends responses.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="list-group-item">
                            <b>Q10.</b> Why are web apps easier to update than desktop apps?
                            <div class="mt-2">
                                <div>A) Update once on server, everyone gets it</div>
                                <div>B) Users reinstall daily</div>
                                <div>C) No code is needed</div>
                                <div>D) Browsers update your database automatically</div>
                                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="mcq10">Show Answer</button>
                                <div id="mcq10" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-success">
                                    <b>Answer:</b> A) Update once on server, everyone gets it<br />
                                    <span class="soft">
                                        Deployment happens on the server side.
                                        Users simply refresh the site and get the latest version instantly.
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
