            <section id="interview" class="card mb-3">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h5">Interview Questions (10) + Answers</h2>
                    <p class="soft">Click “Show Answer” to reveal each answer.</p>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>1) Define a web application.</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv1">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv1" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                A web application is software hosted on a server and accessed through a browser.
                                It handles user actions through HTTP requests and returns responses like HTML or JSON.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>2) Website vs web application—what’s the key difference?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv2">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv2" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                Websites are often informational and may be static.
                                Web applications are interactive and data-driven—logins, workflows, and database updates are common.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>3) What is an HTTP request and response?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv3">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv3" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                A request is sent by the client asking for a resource or action.
                                A response is sent by the server containing output data and status codes such as 200, 404, or 500.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>4) Why is HTTPS important?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv4">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv4" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                HTTPS encrypts communication and protects credentials and sensitive data.
                                It’s essential for secure login, payments, and user trust, and most modern browsers enforce it.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>5) What are typical components of a web application?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv5">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv5" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                Client UI (browser), server application (logic), database (storage), and integrations (APIs, email/SMS, payments).
                                Logging and monitoring are also standard in production.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>6) What is a session or cookie?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv6">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv6" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                Cookies store small client-side data (often an identifier/token).
                                Sessions store server-side user state linked to that identifier and are commonly used after login.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>7) Why do web apps need input validation?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv7">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv7" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                Inputs come from the internet and can be manipulated.
                                Validation prevents errors and protects against attacks like SQL Injection and XSS.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>8) What is the role of a web server (like IIS)?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv8">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv8" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                A web server accepts HTTP requests and forwards them to the application.
                                It manages hosting concerns like ports, SSL, process management, and request routing to the app runtime.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card mb-2">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>9) What is a REST API in the context of web apps?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv9">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv9" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border">
                                A REST API exposes endpoints that return data (usually JSON) instead of HTML.
                                Web apps often call APIs from UI screens to load data asynchronously.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <b>10) How does this connect to ASP.NET MVC?</b><br />
                            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-dark mt-2 qa-btn" data-target="iv10">Show Answer</button>
                            <div id="iv10" class="answer mt-2 alert alert-light border mb-0">
                                ASP.NET MVC is a server-side framework for building web applications.
                                It helps organize code into Controllers (requests), Views (HTML), and Models (data/rules).
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- K) Summary + Next Steps -->
            <section class="card mb-3">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h5">Summary + Next Steps</h2>
                    <ul class="mb-2">
                        <li>A web application runs on a server and is used via a browser.</li>
                        <li>Communication happens through HTTP request/response.</li>
                        <li>Web apps are interactive, dynamic, and often database-driven.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="alert alert-primary mb-0">
                        <b>Next step:</b> Understand what an “ASP.NET Web Application” is and how it differs from other .NET app types.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

